<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bashkirs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bashkort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bashkirs are a Turkic people of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ural-mountains">Ural Mountains</a> and adjacent plains in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, most of whom live in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bashkortostan">Republic of Bashkortostan</a>. Traditionally semi-nomadic herders and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> Muslims, they came under Russian rule in the 1550s and rose repeatedly against colonisation in the 17th and 18th centuries. Bashkir nationalists won an autonomous republic in 1919.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bashkirs.jpg" alt="Bashkirs" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: multiple Автор: Conscious · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Bashkortostan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
